{
  "id": "residual_promote",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "depends_on": [
    "core"
  ],
  "description": "PROMOTE + make-actionable: the missing successor named by refusal_representable.json. A Residual node -- minted by a HEARD refusal (refusal_query_mints_residual, the refusal-selector tie) OR by a perception HOLE (an eye-view field the sensor left un-carved) -- is routed through the EXISTING human-gated self-improvement spine. promote_residual_to_self_concern mints a SelfConcern{source:'residual'} (the SAME node shape gap_awareness.json / conversation_self_concern.json mint, so jabberwock_daemon.py::promote_self_concern -> StandingConcern and reflective_faculty._run_self_gaps both find it), DISTINCT from every ordinary concern (source='residual', kind='residual', the about_residual edge). The DECISION is the graph's (a rule with a content-dedup + mint-once guard, exactly like every gap rule); the human gate stays -- the SelfConcern is filed 'noted', NEVER 'pending'. perception_hole_mints_residual makes the eye-view rung's un-carved HOLE (uncarved_count>0) ACTIONABLE: it fires on REAL hole structure (NOT a rare tie) and NOT on the FLAT space-constancy case (uncarved_count=0 is correct 'nothing here', not a residual). DEFAULT-OFF: inert on any graph without the attends/has_residual edges (no committed seed makes them) -- byte-identity holds.",
  "microtheory": "refusal_capacity",
  "nodes": [],
  "edges": [],
  "productions": [],
  "rules": [
    {
      "name": "perception_hole_mints_residual",
      "comment": "The eye-view rung ALREADY renders the un-carved HOLE (its 9 right-edge cells) as gaps; this makes it ACTIONABLE. A VisionField the agent attends whose carve left un-carved cells (uncarved_count>0) mints ONE Residual{kind:uncarved_hole}. Mint-once via hole_residual_minted. Does NOT fire on FLAT space-constancy (uncarved_count=0: every cell is the one reference group; correct 'nothing here' is not a residual).",
      "match_type": null,
      "match": [
        [
          "agent",
          "attends",
          "field"
        ]
      ],
      "where": {
        "type": "And",
        "items": [
          {
            "type": "Gt",
            "a": {
              "type": "Attr",
              "node": {
                "type": "Var",
                "name": "field"
              },
              "key": "uncarved_count"
            },
            "b": {
              "type": "Lit",
              "value": 0.0
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "Not",
            "arg": {
              "type": "Eq",
              "a": {
                "type": "Attr",
                "node": {
                  "type": "Var",
                  "name": "field"
                },
                "key": "hole_residual_minted"
              },
              "b": {
                "type": "Lit",
                "value": 1.0
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "effects": [
        [
          "set_attr",
          "field",
          "hole_residual_minted",
          1.0
        ],
        [
          "add_node",
          "res",
          "Residual",
          {
            "kind": {
              "__term__": {
                "type": "Lit",
                "value": "uncarved_hole"
              }
            },
            "source_count": {
              "__term__": {
                "type": "Attr",
                "node": {
                  "type": "Var",
                  "name": "field"
                },
                "key": "uncarved_count"
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        [
          "add_edge",
          "field",
          "has_residual",
          "res",
          {}
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "promote_residual_to_self_concern",
      "comment": "THE LOOP CLOSURE. The agent attends a source h that holds a Residual res (the h -has_residual-> res edge refusal_query_mints_residual and perception_hole_mints_residual both mint). File it as a SelfConcern{source:'residual'} the human-gated promote spine can carry -- DISTINCT from every ordinary concern (source/kind/about_residual). Guards: mint-once (res.promoted) + content-dedup (no SelfConcern with equal content) -- the SAME shape every gap_awareness rule carries, so the loop never floods. Filed 'noted', NEVER 'pending': the promote to StandingConcern is the human step (promote_self_concern).",
      "match_type": null,
      "match": [
        [
          "agent",
          "attends",
          "h"
        ],
        [
          "h",
          "has_residual",
          "res"
        ]
      ],
      "where": {
        "type": "And",
        "items": [
          {
            "type": "Not",
            "arg": {
              "type": "Eq",
              "a": {
                "type": "Attr",
                "node": {
                  "type": "Var",
                  "name": "res"
                },
                "key": "promoted"
              },
              "b": {
                "type": "Lit",
                "value": 1.0
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "Not",
            "arg": {
              "type": "Exists",
              "source": {
                "type": "NodesOfType",
                "node_type": "SelfConcern"
              },
              "var_name": "sc2",
              "predicate": {
                "type": "Eq",
                "a": {
                  "type": "Attr",
                  "node": {
                    "type": "Var",
                    "name": "sc2"
                  },
                  "key": "content"
                },
                "b": {
                  "type": "StringConcat",
                  "parts": [
                    {
                      "type": "Lit",
                      "value": "unresolved residual: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "Attr",
                      "node": {
                        "type": "Var",
                        "name": "res"
                      },
                      "key": "kind"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "effects": [
        [
          "set_attr",
          "res",
          "promoted",
          1.0
        ],
        [
          "add_node",
          "sc",
          "SelfConcern",
          {
            "status": "noted",
            "source": "residual",
            "kind": "residual",
            "content": {
              "__term__": {
                "type": "StringConcat",
                "parts": [
                  {
                    "type": "Lit",
                    "value": "unresolved residual: "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "Attr",
                    "node": {
                      "type": "Var",
                      "name": "res"
                    },
                    "key": "kind"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            "residual_kind": {
              "__term__": {
                "type": "Attr",
                "node": {
                  "type": "Var",
                  "name": "res"
                },
                "key": "kind"
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        [
          "add_edge",
          "agent",
          "has_self_concern",
          "sc"
        ],
        [
          "add_edge",
          "sc",
          "about_residual",
          "res",
          {}
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "retire_duplicate_residual_concern",
      "batch": false,
      "comment": "NO FLOOD, part 2 (the gap_awareness retire_duplicate_gap precedent). The mint-rule content-dedup guard only blocks a NEW same-content SelfConcern across passes; two DISTINCT residuals of the same kind minted in ONE pass both file before either sees the other. This retires the duplicates: BATCH-SAFE with no node-id -- the survivor is Argmin over the same-content active residual SelfConcerns (Argmin returns exactly one element from a fixed snapshot within a pass), and a residual SelfConcern is retired (status='retired' + del_edge has_self_concern) iff it is NOT identity-equal to that survivor. A unique concern is its own Argmin survivor, so it is never retired. Scoped to source='residual' so the human-gated conversation concerns are never auto-retired. Runs in the agent's own run_rules fixpoint.",
      "match_type": null,
      "match": [
        [
          "agent",
          "has_self_concern",
          "sc"
        ]
      ],
      "where": {
        "type": "And",
        "items": [
          {
            "type": "Not",
            "arg": {
              "type": "Eq",
              "a": {
                "type": "Attr",
                "node": {
                  "type": "Var",
                  "name": "sc"
                },
                "key": "status"
              },
              "b": {
                "type": "Lit",
                "value": "retired"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "Eq",
            "a": {
              "type": "Attr",
              "node": {
                "type": "Var",
                "name": "sc"
              },
              "key": "source"
            },
            "b": {
              "type": "Lit",
              "value": "residual"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "Not",
            "arg": {
              "type": "Eq",
              "a": {
                "type": "Var",
                "name": "sc"
              },
              "b": {
                "type": "Argmin",
                "source": {
                  "type": "Filter",
                  "source": {
                    "type": "NodesOfType",
                    "node_type": "SelfConcern"
                  },
                  "var_name": "y",
                  "predicate": {
                    "type": "And",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "type": "Eq",
                        "a": {
                          "type": "Attr",
                          "node": {
                            "type": "Var",
                            "name": "y"
                          },
                          "key": "content"
                        },
                        "b": {
                          "type": "Attr",
                          "node": {
                            "type": "Var",
                            "name": "sc"
                          },
                          "key": "content"
                        }
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "Eq",
                        "a": {
                          "type": "Attr",
                          "node": {
                            "type": "Var",
                            "name": "y"
                          },
                          "key": "source"
                        },
                        "b": {
                          "type": "Lit",
                          "value": "residual"
                        }
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "Not",
                        "arg": {
                          "type": "Eq",
                          "a": {
                            "type": "Attr",
                            "node": {
                              "type": "Var",
                              "name": "y"
                            },
                            "key": "status"
                          },
                          "b": {
                            "type": "Lit",
                            "value": "retired"
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                "var_name": "z",
                "value": {
                  "type": "Var",
                  "name": "z"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "effects": [
        [
          "set_attr",
          "sc",
          "status",
          "retired"
        ],
        [
          "del_edge",
          "agent",
          "has_self_concern",
          "sc"
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}
